00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:21.270
- Summit Fever was an amazing experience.

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:23.610
So it's a, it's a mountain climbing movie

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:25.560
and we shot it in Chamonix France,

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:26.700
on top of Mont Blanc

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:29.790
which is one of the largest
mountains in the world.

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:32.310
The fact that we were shooting
it during Covid was amazing

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:34.950
because we had that mountain to ourselves,

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:36.090
which is like,

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:38.580
you would never have a scenario
like that again, you know?

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:40.440
And so there were times
where we're looking around.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.550
We had a very small crew

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:43.350
because when you're
doing this type of film,

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:44.850
you only bring essential elements

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:46.560
up at that kind of altitude.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:47.610
It really took me back

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:50.220
to the reasons why I be
wanted to become an actor,

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:53.490
to have those rare
experiences like that, yeah.

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:54.810
- It is cool what y'all get to do,

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:56.640
or like study for, like
if you're playing a role,

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:58.050
it's a really, it's a really cool job

00:00:58.050 --> 00:00:59.520
because you get to learn a
little bit about everything.

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:01.470
- Yeah. Well, specific to "Summit Fever",

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:02.880
one of the reasons I took the job is

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:05.290
because I always wanted to
learn mountain climbing.

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:07.980
It terrified me, but like,
it was something that,

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:10.320
a skill that I wanted to have a sense of.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:11.880
And man, I'll tell you,

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:13.950
the first climb that I had,

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:15.750
like, I literally started shaking,

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:17.250
like, I have to focus.

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:18.360
I mean, that's all legit.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:19.680
The icicles on my,

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:21.694
That's not makeup you
guys, that's, that's,

00:01:21.694 --> 00:01:23.610
that's really what we were going through.

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:25.380
So when you do a mountain climbing movie

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:27.870
on an independent budget,
there's no green screen.

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:29.250
There's no special effects.

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:32.220
So all the stuff we're doing
in that movie is legitimate,

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:34.620
and the ice climbs were terrifying.

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:35.700
Absolutely terrifying.

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:36.533
- Yeah. Nothing

00:01:36.533 --> 00:01:40.200
about anything you just
said sounds exciting to me.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.820
It sounds exciting to watch,

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:42.653
you do.

00:01:42.653 --> 00:01:43.486
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:43.486 --> 00:01:45.360
It's not for everybody, obviously,

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:48.150
and I'm a bit of an adrenaline
junkie, thrill seeker

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:49.800
so, I loved it.

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:51.240
And it's something that
I will continue to do.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:52.260
I, I really dug it.

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:53.250
- That's really cool.

